WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.720
The wildly talented cast of Knives Out consists
of former superheroes, super spies, and a

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:11.170
few legendary Hollywood superstars like Jamie
Lee Curtis, Don Johnson, and Michael Shannon

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.360
— to name only a few!

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.490
But where have you seen the rest of these
familiar faces before?

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.670
Well, here's a handy who's who for Rian Johnson's
whodunnit, Knives Out.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.160
Unless you've been living under a rock for
the past decade, chances are good that you're

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.359
familiar with Daniel Craig and his prestigious
body of work.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:32.790
The English actor's breakout role was that
of the iconic 00 Agent, James Bond, in 2006's

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.030
Casino Royale.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.260
It was a role that, thanks to multiple sequels,
landed him on Forbes' World's Highest Paid

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.620
Actors list in 2015.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.179
However, the handsome Brit is far from a one-trick
pony.

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:47.300
Over the years, Craig has excelled in a vast
array of genres, ranging from dramas like

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.430
2002's Oscar-winning Road to Perdition to
comedies like 2017's Logan Lucky.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.100
In Knives Out, Craig plays Benoit Blanc, a
private detective brought on to investigate

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.120
the death of famous crime novelist Harlan
Thrombey.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.760
"I suspect foul play.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.360
I have eliminated no suspects."

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.530
Craig was actually the first actor to sign
on to the project, and he was apparently flattered

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.750
to have been offered the part.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.100
As he explained to Cinema Blend,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.980
"I hadn't read something like that before,
and I was just over the moon that [Johnson]

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:16.980
offered it to me."

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.400
With a lead like Craig, it's no mystery why
so many critics are crazy about Knives Out.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.240
Agatha Christie lovers ... assemble!

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.100
Although the MCU's Captain America obviously
won't be making an appearance in Johnson's

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.570
murder mystery, Chris Evans, who's played
the star-spangled Avenger several times since

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.640
2011's Captain America: The First Avenger,
will be.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:41.100
The Boston-bred hunk has flexed his dramatic
ability in films like Before We Go and Gifted,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.540
but not as often as he's flexed his impressive
physique in action flicks The Losers and Scott

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.200
Pilgrim vs. the World.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.980
With an apparent affinity for playing "the
good guy," Evans has played not one but two

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.340
different superheroes, first starring as the
Human Torch in the Fantastic Four franchise.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.820
His role of Ransom Drysdale in Knives Out,
however, will be quite the opposite.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.210
Evans told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.080
"I'm usually tasked with playing guys who
are a little more noble, and this guy is a

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.090
little bit more vile.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.080
It's fun."

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:12.629
Although it didn't exactly light up the box
office, 1992's The Efficiency Expert, starring

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:17.569
acting legends like Anthony Hopkins and Russell
Crowe marked the film debut of Toni Collette.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:22.159
In the decades to come, the Australian actress
would enjoy a highly successful career, most

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.640
evidenced by her massive award-season love.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.800
In 2009, she was cast as the lead role in
Showtime's United States of Tara.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:33.720
As Tara, a mother coping with dissociative
identity disorder, Collette earned wins at

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.769
both the Golden Globes and the Emmys.

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:39.980
On the big screen, the actress has excelled
in dramatic comedies like Little Miss Sunshine

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.079
and About a Boy.

00:02:41.079 --> 00:02:45.620
However, she's perhaps most recognized for
her work in a pair of iconic horror flicks:

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:51.040
1999's unforgettably twisty The Sixth Sense
and 2018's disturbingly dark Hereditary.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.400
In Knives Out, the decorated actress plays
Joni Thrombey, a "lifestyle guru" and daughter-in-law

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.640
of murder victim Harlan Thrombey.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.599
When speaking to Deadline, Collette showered
the murder mystery's script with praise, saying,

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.209
"It was all in the writing.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:08.790
In reading it, it just kept opening up and
changing, and it was so swift, and so smooth,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.120
and so surprising."

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.800
What Katherine Langford's filmography lacks
in quantity, it makes up for in quality.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.440
At the ripe age of 20, the young Australian
actress landed the role of ill-fated high

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:23.280
school student Hannah Baker in the Netflix
smash series 13 Reasons Why.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.600
Langford stole the show as Hannah, even earning
a Golden Globe nomination for her performance.

00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:33.129
Her newfound stardom landed her parts in two
movies in 2018, The Misguided and Love, Simon.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.129
"Oh my God.

00:03:34.129 --> 00:03:36.230
Have you guys seen Creek Secrets today?"

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.760
Although she'd previously worked with some
fairly big names, Langford was admittedly

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.930
quite starstruck when seeing her Knives Out
co-stars in action.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.600
She told Yahoo! TV:

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.280
"I get so in awe of everyone.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.719
... I've watched all of these people."

00:03:47.719 --> 00:03:51.690
While sharing the screen with A-listers like
Daniel Craig and Chris Evans must've been

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.340
incredible, the young starlet, who plays Meg
Thrombey in the whodunnit, went on to specifically

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.540
give praise to her fellow Aussie actress.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.360
Calling Toni Collette a, quote, "legend,"
she claimed that working with her was "amazing."

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:09.189
Although her official acting debut came in
a Spanish film in 2006, Ana de Armas' Hollywood

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:14.660
career really started in 2015, starring alongside
Keanu Reeves as Bell in the dark thriller

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.660
Knock Knock.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.120
After that, she played Miles Teller's girlfriend,
Iz, in War Dogs, and then the holographic

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.190
Joi in the trippy Blade Runner 2049.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:28.080
Although she's starring alongside Daniel Craig
in 2020's new Bond film, No Time to Die, the

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.730
gorgeous Cuban starlet first shared the screen
with him in Knives Out.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:36.271
As Marta Cabrera, the recently deceased Harlan
Thrombey's live-in nurse, de Armas is one

00:04:36.271 --> 00:04:37.890
of the prime murder suspects.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.950
But while de Armas admittedly had a wonderful
experience on set, shooting in Boston had

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.450
one particular downside.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.450
She explained:

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.860
"It was my first time in Boston.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:48.140
It was freezing, for a Cuban especially."

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.650
The actress may have been cold, but is she
actually Knives Out's cold-blooded killer?

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.530
Life has been especially good for Lakeith
Stanfield over the past ten years.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:01.670
The California-raised actor's first big break
was getting cast as Marcus in Short Term 12,

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:02.710
alongside Brie Larson.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.850
He then was cast as Jimmie Lee Jackson in
2014's Oscar-winning Martin Luther King Jr.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.800
biopic, Selma.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.360
Since then, his career has really caught fire.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.980
Although he's appeared in popular films like
Get Out, Sorry to Bother You, and Netflix's

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:20.440
Death Note, perhaps his most recognizable
role is that of the philosophical stoner Darius

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.800
in Donald Glover's comedic drama Atlanta.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:27.780
"Not all great things come from great pain.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.800
Sometimes, it's love.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.150
Not everything's a sacrifice."

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.040
For Knives Out, Stanfield is playing Lieutenant
Elliot, a detective investigating Harlan Thrombey's

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.840
death.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.800
Though he initially thinks that the victim
took his own life, more clues begin to surface

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.770
— and his character starts to suspect something
more sinister is afoot.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:51.180
The award-winning actor will, much like the
audience, try to solve Rian Johnson's whodunnit.

